{%- comment -%}
  ORI redesign — fallback for the GVM stage summary. When a product has no
  stage_summary metafield (e.g. on a store imported without metafields), its
  description carries the same content as HTML:

    <p>Chevrolet Silverado 1500 ZR2.</p>
    <ul><li><strong>GVM:</strong> 3650kg | <strong>GCM:</strong> 7160kg …</li> …</ul>
    <p>Wheels and tyres not included.</p>

  This flattens it into the line format snippets/ori-gvm-summary.liquid reads
  (one line per paragraph, "- " in front of each list item), separated with
  <br /> so it splits exactly like a newline_to_br'd metafield.

  Accepts:
  - html: {String} product.description
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign t = html | strip_newlines
  assign t = t | replace: '<li>', '¦- ' | replace: '<li ', '¦- <li '
  assign t = t | replace: '</li>', '¦' | replace: '</p>', '¦' | replace: '<br>', '¦' | replace: '<br/>', '¦' | replace: '<br />', '¦'
  assign t = t | replace: '</h2>', '¦' | replace: '</h3>', '¦' | replace: '</h4>', '¦'
  assign t = t | strip_html | replace: '&nbsp;', ' '
  echo t | replace: '¦', '<br />'
-%}
